*Variables in a REST pipeline

  Two rules make variables the natural way to pass request state between functions.

  First, the HTTP request body can be read only once.  Only one function may bind <<<@RequestBody>>>.  When a
  later function also needs the body, the first function binds it once and publishes it with <<<Out>>>.  The later
  function reads the variable, not the body.

  Second, <<<@Val>>> returns the same object the producer stored.  It is not a copy.  So one function can load
  an entity into a variable, a second function can mutate that entity in place, and a third function sees the
  change.

  The {{{../SpringRestCrudHttpServer/index.html}REST CRUD Orchestration}} tutorial uses both rules to build
  a full resource.  The {{{../SpringRestOrchestrationReference/index.html}Orchestration Patterns and Naming}}
  reference states them in full.



